From 4252b6008da1849e1e546e519bc9eb1f0c4784ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:52:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): keep default profile for connection-tagged rows
 in archive preflight [daveey]

Review of 41c9fdb0db found that the invocation's active profile was borrowed for
every row with no resolvable profile, including a row that already carries its own
remote connection_id. Such a row was safety-read and PATCHed under the window's
active profile on another gateway (hermes-hub/work instead of hermes-hub/default).

Cause (happened): captureArchiveOwner pins the registry primary onto an ownerless
row, so archivePreflight could no longer tell a pinned connection from the row's
own, and applied the fallback to both. Cause (not caught): tests covered only the
unlisted ownerless case.

- captureArchiveOwner records primary-pinned rows; archivePreflight uses the
  invocation profile only for those, and 'default' for a row with its own connection.
- The overall preflight timer trails the capped per-request timeout by 250ms, so the
  last reconnect attempt's transport rejection wins the race and is restored with an
  error instead of becoming a Task-status-unavailable override dialog. The trace text
  now reports the real limit.
- Tests: own-connection row stays on default under an active nondefault profile (RED
  on 41c9fdb0db); profile switched while resolution is pending (kills the
  read-after-await mutant); rejection 1ms and 30ms after the capped timeout.
